# Guide / training text PDFs

Companion inventory + quality bar: [`docs/audit/guide-pdf-quality-2026-08.md`](../../docs/audit/guide-pdf-quality-2026-08.md).

## Hard rules

1. **Shared chrome only** — pocket sheets, floor checklists, bylaws sheets, steward workspace PDFs, and certificates draw through [`text-pdf-layout.ts`](../../src/lib/export/text-pdf-layout.ts) (or certificate helpers that reuse the same mark loader). Do not reintroduce a private Helvetica-only `writeSimplePdf`.
2. **Platform awareness** — header embeds UnionOps mark PNG (`UNIONOPS_LOGOS.markInterlock`). Keep the education footer wordmark (“UnionOps … education only”). Do not rely on centered Helvetica `UNIONOPS` as the only brand signal.
3. **Local vs platform** — header = UnionOps platform mark. Subtitle/local line = Brand Kit local number. Certificates may add optional Brand Kit (local) logo as secondary — never replace the platform mark with a local logo alone.
4. **Dynamic-import jsPDF** inside the export path (`TOOL-004`). Wrap UI triggers in `useExportHandler` + user-visible error.
5. **EN + FR** education footers and localized sheet copy stay in sync on claim (see `i18n-public-copy.mdc`).
6. **Do not rebrand** static Ontario ministry PDFs under `public/assets/ontario-board-posters/`.
7. **Canvas Comms PDFs** stay on `pdf-export.ts` + Phase 9 fidelity — do not route them through text-PDF layout.
8. **Brand Kit faces when provided** — register OFL TTFs via `registerGuidePdfFonts`; system faces stay Helvetica. Locale follows UI `en` | `fr`. OOXML binary embed remains deferred (B3).

## Tests

- Unit: layout helpers + worksheet layout contracts (`text-pdf-layout.test.ts`, `worksheet-pdf-test-helpers.test.ts`, `land-acknowledgement-worksheet-pdf.test.ts`) + certificate dual-logo placement (`certificate.test.ts`).
- Smoke: `e2e/guide-pdf.export.smoke.spec.ts` — real download, size floor, pdf.js text (title + footer), embedded mark image.
- Text PDFs are **not** canvas `compareRasters` targets.

## When adding a new guide handout PDF

1. Add export to the inventory table in the audit doc.
2. **Checklist sheets** → `writeBrandedChecklistPdf`. **Fill-in worksheets** (ruled rows, inline fields, sign-off) → `writeBrandedWorksheetPdf` — see layout model in `text-pdf-layout.ts` (`sections` + optional `closingSections` + pinned footer band). **Long-form notes** → `writeBrandedNotesPdf`. No one-off jsPDF letter loops.
3. Worksheet primitives: `field` / `fieldPair`, `ruled` with optional `fill: true`, `check` / `checkPair`. One `fill` block per sheet; pin review checklists in `closingSections`.
4. Extend unit content contracts and at least one smoke download path if the CTA is new on a guide page.
5. Steward-visible capability → What's new note (`whats-new.mdc`).
